# Move a Thread to the trash, and print its threadId as JSON
# The threadId is printed by the other gmail-thread commands
# Gmail purges a trashed Thread after 30 days. Restore it within that time with gmail-thread-untrash
# There is no command to delete a Thread for good
# Errors:
# GMAIL_THREAD_ID_MISSING   The threadId is empty
# GMAIL_THREAD_NOT_FOUND    The Thread does not exist
# Flags:
# --account <name>     Account of the Thread. The default account if empty
# Usage:
# $ gmail-thread-trash threadId
# $ gmail-thread-trash threadId --account perso
setopt local_options err_return

local libDir="${functions_source[$0]:A:h:h}/__lib"
node "${libDir}/bin/gmail-thread-trash.js" "$@"
